  "title": "End-Devouring Rays",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Problem Let $G$ be a graph, $\\omega$ a countable end of $G$, and $K$ an infinite set of pairwise disjoint $\\omega$-rays in $G$. Prove that there is a set $K'$ of pairwise disjoint $\\omega$-rays that devours $\\omega$ such that the set of starting vertices of rays in $K'$ equals the set of starting vertices of rays in $K$.",
